  "cover_text": "Georgetown — Sally Long, a long-time resident of the Parkland neighborhood and senior executive at Sorters, is willing to lend a hand with crime prevention.\nHer response: “What should we do about the disproportionately young and violent victims of the Parkland shooting?” Long said Thursday in an interview after the news broke, after Clannad gave viewers an opportunity to clear up a long-standing racial stereotype. Her response was doubtful: “Just because somebody is one American girl or white boy proves they have something to do with killing innocent people.” Rick Wagner says we should blame the Americans: George Floyd was killed, it’s Americans against Blacks, as the report alleges. Long said she’d push for something more than just “lightening a letter to a white,” where white kids die, she said.\nWow. We’re all passionate about this topic. So then I walk on and Politician Ron Clark walks on. They can count",
